## ACCEPTANCE TESTS (manual, on tablet)
1. Header "Layers" opens the panel with "Layer 1" highlighted as active. ＋ adds "Layer 2" at the top and makes it active.
2. Draw on Layer 2, tap Layer 1, draw again. Hide Layer 2 (👁): its strokes disappear; Show brings them back.
3. Lock Layer 1: drawing on it shows toast "Layer is locked"; its strokes can't be erased, selected, or picked with the eyedropper. Unlock restores this.
4. Select strokes (Select tool) -> in the panel tap ⇥ on another layer: strokes move (one Undo moves them back). Hidden/locked target shows a toast.
5. Hiding or locking a layer drops its strokes from the current selection.
6. Rename (✎) updates the name. ↑/↓ reorders rows (drawing result unchanged).
7. Delete a layer with strokes: strokes vanish; Undo restores the layer AND its strokes. Deleting the last layer shows "Cannot delete the last layer".
8. Add layer then Undo: the layer disappears and the active layer falls back to an existing one.
9. Save, Clear strokes, Open: layers (names, hidden, locked) and stroke assignment are restored. Old 0.x-1.1 files load with all strokes on "Layer 1".
10. Color wheel: tap the toolbar color circle -> popover. Drag on the ring changes hue, drag in the square changes saturation/brightness; the toolbar circle and next stroke use the color. Typing a valid #rrggbb in the HEX box updates the wheel. Finished picks appear as recent dots (max 8, newest first).
11. Eyedropper a stroke while the popover is open: the wheel jumps to that color; picking a gray/black keeps the previous hue.

